//
// Conduit (--use-conduit --conduit-fuse-channels-flag) end-to-end run for
// `--conduit-fuse-channels` (channel-fusion annotation pass).  E2E
// companion to lit-only pin
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/conduit_fuse_channels.mlir
// and Python-harness sibling
//   iron_operator_mlir/fusion_npu_regression/fuse_channels_smoke.py.
//
// Pre-pass: 4 conduits in one device on one tile (tile(0,2)) — `@ext_in_a`
// and `@ext_in_d` produced by shim, `@inter` self-loop on tile(0,2),
// `@ext_out` produced by tile(0,2) to shim.  Add → Mul chain inside one
// core's body block (Add: ext_in_a + 1.0 → inter; Mul: inter * ext_in_d →
// ext_out), sequenced so the two PRODUCER-side conduits on tile(0,2) —
// `@inter` and `@ext_out` — have non-overlapping live windows in the same
// parent block.  After `--conduit-fuse-channels` (injected by `--conduit-
// fuse-channels-flag`, see `aiecc.cpp:1515`) those two producer-side
// conduits are stamped with matching `dma_channel_group="groupN"` and
// `fuse_mode="static"` annotations.  Pass C downstream consumes the
// annotations to fold the grouped conduits onto a single HW DMA channel.
// IR shape is otherwise unchanged — fuse-channels is annotation-only.
// Single-column smoke uses `npu2_1col`.
//
// Why ONLY `--conduit-fuse-channels-flag` (no `--conduit-fuse-spatial`,
// no `--conduit-fuse-core-bodies-flag`): the pass groups producer-side
// conduits already co-located on the same tile by the source IR shape;
// it does NOT require `--aie-combine-device` to merge separate `aie.device`
// blocks.  No `fusion_group=` annotation is set in the source IR — that
// attribute is the pairing key for fuse-operators / fuse-core-bodies, NOT
// fuse-channels.  Fuse-channels groups by (producer-tile, parent-block,
// window-disjointness) discovered automatically.
//
// PASS expectation: every dispatch (4 invocations) completes; output bytes
// match reference computed by test.cpp (out[j] = (in_a[j]+1.0)*in_d[j],
// in_a[j] = (j%16), in_d[j] = 2.0 — equivalent to (j%16+1)*2).  Because
// fuse-channels is annotation-only, output MUST also be byte-identical to
// a bare `--use-conduit` pipeline (no fuse-channels flag) on the same IR;
// any divergence is a Pass C consumer-side bug surfaced by the grouping
// annotation.  Failure modes that lit-only fixtures cannot catch (per
// fuse_channels_smoke.py docstring):
//   * Annotation present + Pass C HW-channel folding emits clean IR but
//     the grouped channels mis-route on hardware (silent wrong output:
//     out_a routed to out_b's slot, etc.).  Lit verifies annotation
//     presence and Pass C compile-clean shape; only an end-to-end byte
//     check catches mis-routing.
//   * `dma_channel_group` annotation confuses Pass C lowering — e.g., the
//     consumer-side BD chain of `@inter` (tile→tile self-loop) or the
//     shim-bound `@ext_out` becomes inconsistent post-fold, producing
//     all-zero or garbled output across dispatches.
//   * Multi-block / re-acquire stability — the pass is documented as
//     idempotent (the lit pin runs `--conduit-fuse-channels` twice for
//     this reason).  Per-launch re-acquire of grouped channels across
//     `NUM_INVOCATIONS=4` is what surfaces idempotency-edge bugs that
//     a single-dispatch lit fixture would silently hide.
//
// Sibling references:
//   * `test/npu-xrt/fuse_operators_basic_npu/conduit.lit` — same Add → Mul
//     1:1 chain at the IR level but with the `--conduit-fuse-spatial`
//     pipeline (separate-device pre-fuse, two-column post-fuse).  This
//     fixture's single-device IR shape is what makes the fuse-channels
//     producer-side grouping eligible — diffing the two fixtures'
//     post-compile IR isolates which behavior is contributed by spatial
//     fusion vs. channel fusion.
//   * `test/npu-xrt/fuse_core_bodies_npu/conduit.lit` — same Add → Mul
//     1:1 chain with the hybrid `--conduit-fuse-core-bodies-flag
//     --conduit-fuse-spatial` pipeline that collapses both cores onto one
//     tile via `--aie-combine-device same-tile=true`.  fuse-channels
//     reaches a similar single-tile producer-side IR shape from the
//     OPPOSITE direction (single-device source vs. spatially-fused merge).
//   * `test/npu-xrt/fuse_operators_convergent_npu/conduit.lit` —
//     convergent K=2 fuse-operators reference for the canonical 3-file
//     fixture pattern (aie.mlir / test.cpp / conduit.lit + REQUIRES /
//     RUN-line skeleton this fixture follows).
//   * `test/Dialect/Conduit/conduit_fuse_channels.mlir` — canonical lit-
//     only pin for `--conduit-fuse-channels` (19 cases a-s covering all
//     analysis edge cases; runs the pass twice to verify idempotency).
//
// No stateful companion: the source IR uses Conduit-only annotation
// semantics (`dma_channel_group`, `fuse_mode`) that have no stateful
// objectfifo equivalent.  Reference is computed in test.cpp.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Kernel compute is inlined bf16 add + multiply.  Chess (xchesscc) cannot
// select `fp_to_bf16` for this inline core (`fatal error: error in
// backend: Cannot select: i32 = fp_to_bf16`); Peano can.  Use
// `--no-xchesscc --no-xbridge` to route the kernel compile through Peano
// (sibling pattern: `convergent_npu/conduit.lit`,
// `fuse_operators_basic_npu/conduit.lit`, `fuse_core_bodies_npu/
// conduit.lit`, `loadpdi/run.lit`, `vec_vec_add_objfifo_init/aie2.py`).
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --no-xchesscc --no-xbridge --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --conduit-fuse-channels-flag --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
